From 826ee9a8f56aafe843cb3099a6a40476d707b68f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AF9 <af9@localhost>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 14:29:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] KubeJS recipes: a bad recipe fails alone

GT 7.5 throws from the recipe builders on an unknown or empty item / fluid, and KubeJS (2001.6.5-build.16) posts
the recipe event without an exception handler: the first throw ended the event, and every recipe script after the
one that threw added nothing. A pack whose scripts were written for 7.2 (which took such a recipe and let it fail
on its own) lost most of its recipes to one stale id.

- GTRecipeSchema: the item / fluid validation reports the id and leaves the builder call; the recipe fails with
  that message when it is built (KubeJS counts it as a failed recipe), the script goes on.
- RecipesEventJSMixin: the recipe event is posted with an exception handler, so any other error in a recipe script
  ends that script only.
- Version 7.5.3-af9.2.
